Here is the reformatted code:

Algorithm 3 Hierarchical-Sampling-Preprocessing
Input: D
Output: G(D)

1: for i from 1 to k do
2:     sample |L_i| points from D
3:     foreach point p in L_i do
4:         compute nearest neighbor q in L_{i-1}
5:         add edge (p, q) to G(D)
6:     update area sets and enclosing balls for L_i

Algorithm 4 Hierarchical-Sampling-Query
Input: G(D), S\ud835\udc53,\u2113,\ud835\udc62
Output: D\ud835\udc5c=S\ud835\udc53,\u2113,\ud835\udc62\u2229D

1: for i from k to 1 do
2:     foreach point p in L_i do
3:         if B(\ud835\udc50\ud835\udc4e\ud835\udc5b\ud835\udc51\ud835\udc56\ud835\udc51\ud835\udc4e\ud835\udc61\ud835\udc52\ud835\udc60)(p) ∩ S = \u2200 then
4:             prune node p from further exploration
5:         else
6:             explore neighbors of p in next lower layer

Note that the exact implementation details are not provided, but the above code outlines the general structure of the algorithms.
